From 0e17c7fd3e1a4f814fd47ded122c4c47382899c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Letian Kang <Letian.Kang@amd.com>
Date: Sat, 13 Jun 2026 14:44:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] amdsmi: add WSL2 (DirectX/dxgkrnl) GPU support via HIP
 runtime fallback

On WSL2, AMD GPUs are exposed through the DirectX paravirtualization
layer (/dev/dxg) rather than the native amdgpu/KFD stack, so /dev/kfd and
the amdgpu sysfs nodes are absent. As a result rsmi_init() fails during
KFD node discovery and amdsmi_init() returns DRIVER_NOT_LOADED, leaving
callers (and the amd-smi CLI) with no usable device.

This adds an optional, self-contained WSL2 fallback that is engaged only
when the host is detected as WSL2 and the native rsmi/KFD discovery has
failed, so it has zero effect on bare-metal Linux:

- New amd_smi_wsl.{h,cc}: detect WSL2 (microsoft/WSL kernel marker +
  /dev/dxg present + /dev/kfd absent); enumerate GPUs and query static
  info through the HIP runtime, dlopen'd lazily via the existing library
  loader (no hard link against HIP, no torch). Only forward-ABI-stable
  HIP entry points are used (hipGetDeviceCount, hipDeviceGetName,
  hipDeviceGetPCIBusId, hipMemGetInfo, hipDeviceGetAttribute, ...),
  avoiding version-dependent structs such as hipDeviceProp_t.
- AMDSmiGPUDevice: WSL constructor that skips drm/ualoe init; is_wsl()/
  get_wsl_info(); get_mutex() falls back to a static mutex on WSL.
- AMDSmiSystem: populate_amd_gpu_devices_wsl() hooked into the discovery
  failure path; gpu_wsl_mode_ flag so cleanup() skips rsmi_shut_down().
- amd_smi.cc: WSL branches for get_gpu_{asic,board,vram_info,vram_usage,
  memory_total,memory_usage,device_uuid,process_list}_info. Fields with a
  HIP data source (market name, vendor, BDF, VRAM total/used, compute
  units, UUID) are populated; telemetry with no WSL2 data source (power,
  temperature, fan, clocks) keeps returning NOT_SUPPORTED.
- amdsmi_cli/amdsmi_init.py: check_wsl2_gpu() so the CLI initializes with
  INIT_AMD_GPUS on WSL2 instead of exiting with 'amdgpu not found'.

Validated on a Radeon 8060S (gfx1151) APU under WSL2 + ROCm 7.2.4:
amd-smi list/static/metric and the Python amdsmi interface report the
device, VRAM usage and compute units with no errors.
